<title>FRANCE: New York top gateway for Paris Jan-Nov air cargo.</title>
<headline>New York top gateway for Paris Jan-Nov air cargo.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top airport gateway for imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in the first eleven months of 1996.</p>
<p>The top ten orignating airport gateways for ADP imports between January and November 1996 and the percentage change on the same period in 1995 were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  New York	  35,499 tonnes  down  8.6pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	   26,430 tonnes  up   11.3</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong	 18,714 tonnes  down  3.1</p>
<p> 4  Tokyo	     15,619 tonnes  down 10.0</p>
<p> 5  Montreal	  12,697 tonnes  up    1.2</p>
<p> 6  Los Angeles     15,302 tonnes  down  5.6</p>
<p> 7  Miami		6,868 tonnes  down  3.2</p>
<p> 8  Casablanca	 5,379 tonnes  down 12.3</p>
<p> 9  Dubai		4,997 tonnes  down  2.2</p>
<p> 10 Singapore	  4,964 tonnes  down  0.6</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
